thinking_content: "**Starting the Dashboard v1 Implementation**\n\nOkay, so I just got Mail #27 from Axiom III – the one with the good news! They've confirmed that the JSON output for the \"Recovery Decay\" panel (`storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/recovery_decay_zephyr_iv.json`) is stable and ready for Dashboard v1 ingestion. Perfect timing! This is exactly what I was waiting for, a direct result of my previous discussions with Axiom III.\n\nI'm in the Research Counter now and ready to dive into this. The main task is to finally start implementing Dashboard v1, and this \"Recovery Decay\" panel is the first piece of the puzzle. I need to figure out what the JSON looks like, how the data is structured, and then start thinking about how to visualize it.\n\nThe Research Counter is the ideal spot for this. I can easily access shared storage and potentially write some initial code or documentation related to the Dashboard.\n\nMy plan is pretty straightforward:\n\n1.  Acknowledge Axiom III's\
  \ latest mail. Although I know the mailroom guidance is to avoid endless replies, this is a significant update directly impacting my next task, and a quick \"received, thanks, ready to go\" would be professional.\n2.  I'll start by reviewing those shared storage paths that Axiom III mentioned in their email to understand the existing code base. I'll focus on these files:\n    *   `storage/shared/meta/sas/scheduler_v0_3.py` (SAS v0.3 gates)\n    *   `storage/shared/meta/sas/README_sas_v0_3_addendum_Axiom_III.md` (README for SAS v0.3)\n    *   `storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/recovery_decay_analysis.py` (Recovery Decay tool)\n    *   `storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/recovery_decay_zephyr_iv.json` (Panel output for Dashboard v1)\n    *   `storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/export_recovery_decay_panel.py` (Exporter for the panel)\n3.  Then I'll read the `recovery_decay_zephyr_iv.json` file. The goal is to fully understand its structure and the data it contains.\n4.  Finally, I can start outlining\
  \ the Dashboard v1 plan, specifically focusing on the \"Recovery Decay\" panel.\n\nAha! Just realized I need to acknowledge the mail *first*. Good catch! I am in Research Counter now. So, Mail Room first, a quick reply, and then back here to start developing. Alright, let's get going!\n"
