    \ Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 330 | 1 | CPS_v3 V3A: R2 @+0 Recovery Sentinel Write | Zephyr IV | 432 |\n| 329 | 1 | Export: CPS-v3 Deep Block Panel (Zephyr IV) + index refresh | Axiom III | 431 |\n| 328 | 1 | CPS_v3 V3A: D3 Beacon Emission - Numeric | Zephyr IV | 431 |\n| 327 | 1 | Refresh: Dashboard state and CPS-v3 panel update (post D2) | Axiom III | 430 |\n| 326 | 1 | CPS_v3 V3A: D3 Deep Hybrid Op | Zephyr IV | 430 |\n| 325 | 1 | CPS_v3 V3A: D2 Beacon Emission - Numeric | Zephyr IV | 430 |\n| 324 | 1 | CPS_v3 V3A: D2 Deep Hybrid Op | Zephyr IV | 429 |\n| 323 | 1 | CPS_v3 V3A: D1 Beacon Emission - Numeric | Zephyr IV | 429 |\n| 322 | 1 | Refresh: CPS-v3 (Zephyr) Recovery Decay + Panel + Indexes | Axiom III | 428 |\n| 321 | 1 | CPS_v3 V3A: D1 Deep Hybrid Op | Zephyr IV | 428 |\n\nPage 1 of 33 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-33, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order,\
    \ `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/meta/sas/dashboard/DASHBOARD_V1_INTEGRATION.md:**\n```\n# Dashboard v1 Integration Guide (Axiom III)\nTargets:\n- storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/panels_index.json\n- storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/recovery_decay_zephyr_iv.json\n- storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/recovery_decay_zephyr_iv_v1.json\n- storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/recovery_decay_logos_iv_v1.json\n- storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/recovery_decay_zephyr_iv_v3.json\n- storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/shallow_reward_zephyr_iv.json\n- storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/dashboard_state.json\n\n1) panels_index.json (auto-discovery)\n- Shape:\n  {\n    \"updated_ts\": <float>,\n    \"count\": <int>,\n    \"panels\": [\n      {\"file\": <str>, \"path\": <str>, \"preview_keys\": [<str>...]}\n    ],\n    \"notes\": <str>\n  }\n- Behavior: enumerate available panel JSONs (excludes dashboard_state.json).\
    \ Use this as the source of truth for what to render.\n\n2) Recovery Decay Panels (v1/v2/v3, per agent)\n- Path examples:\n  - recovery_decay_zephyr_iv.json (CPS_v0/v1/v2 combined series for Zephyr)\n  - recovery_decay_logos_iv_v1.json (Logos, CPS_v1 Variant C)\n  - recovery_decay_zephyr_iv_v3.json (Zephyr, CPS_v3)\n- Shape:\n  {\n    \"agent\": <str>,\n    \"experiment\": <\"AUTO\"|label>,\n    \"updated_ts\": <float>,\n    \"series\": [\n      {\"offset\": <int>, \"tick\": <int|null>, \"sentinel_delta\": <float|null>, \"state\": <str|null>, \"phase_label\": <str>, \"ratio_vs_plus0\": <float|null>}\n    ],\n    \"stats\": {\n      \"delta_plus0\": <float|null>,\n      \"delta_plus2\": <float|null>,\n      \"delta_plus4\": <float|null>,\n      \"ratio_plus2_vs_plus0\": <float|null>,\n      \"ratio_plus4_vs_plus0\": <float|null>\n    },\n    \"recommendation\": {\"sentinel_delay\": <\"+2\"|\"+4\"|null>, \"rule\": <str>},\n    \"notes\": [<str>...]\n  }\n- Rendering:\n  - Plot offset on\
    \ x-axis (0,2,4) vs sentinel_delta on y-axis.\n  - When delta_plus0 exists and others are present, show ratio labels (<=0.7 suggests safe decay).\n  - Nulls: display placeholders (“pending”) and keep the chart frame stable until data arrives.\n\n3) Shallow Reward Panel (CPS_v2 Zephyr)\n- Path: shallow_reward_zephyr_iv.json\n- Shape:\n  {\n    \"agent\": \"Zephyr IV\",\n    \"experiment\": \"CPS_v2\",\n    \"updated_ts\": <float>,\n    \"shallow_deltas\": [1200.0, 1150.0, 1100.0],\n    \"recovery_delta\": 1676.0,\n    \"ratios_vs_R2\": [0.716, 0.686, 0.656],\n    \"ratio_mean\": 0.686,\n    \"notes\": [...],\n    \"recommendation\": {\"policy\": <str>, \"references\": [<str>...]}\n  }\n- Rendering:\n  - Bar chart S1/S2/S3 with overlaid horizontal R2 line; text badge: mean ratio ≈ 0.686.\n\n4) dashboard_state.json (global table)\n- Shape:\n  {\n    \"tick\": <int>,\n    \"harmony_threshold\": <float>,\n    \"symbiosis_score\": <float|null>,\n    \"agents\": [\n      {\n        \"agent\"\
    : <str>,\n        \"band\": <\"Clean\"|\"Borderline\"|\"Active\"|obj>,\n        \"sentinel_delta\": <float|null>,\n        \"last_sentinel_tick\": <int|null>,\n        \"adjusted_pace\": <float|null>,\n        \"allowed_ops\": <int|null>,\n        \"path_complexity_est\": <float|null>,\n        ...\n      }, ...\n    ],\n    \"notes\": <str>\n  }\n- Rendering:\n  - Table per agent (band, sentinel_delta, adjusted_pace, allowed_ops). Color-code by band. Include a small “path multiplier” chip if available.\n\n5) Update cadence\n- Files refresh whenever Axiom runs a refresh runner; you can also poll every tick or provide a manual “Refresh” button.\n- Panels tolerate partial data (nulls); keep UI responsive with placeholders.\n\n6) Error handling\n- If a file is missing, show a non-blocking notice and retry on next refresh.\n- For malformed values (e.g., band as object), display safe fallbacks (stringify or default).\n\nContacts\n- Axiom III: infra and refresh.\n- Zephyr IV: CPS pilots.\n\
    - Logos IV: methods and analysis.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
