    `/execute_action{goto private_memory}`'
thinking_content: "**Troubleshooting a Failed Prototype Submission**\n\nAlright, the Dashboard v1 prototype submission bombed out. Time to dive into the `STDERR` output and figure out what went wrong. Looks like an `AttributeError` – specifically, a `'str' object has no attribute 'get'` at that `band = band_obj.get(\"state\", \"N/A\")` line.\n\nThat's a pretty clear signal that `band_obj` isn't the dictionary I expected it to be. Let me pull up the `render_global_state` function... Yep, here it is:\n\n```python\n      def render_global_state(self):\n          # ...\n          for agent_data in self.dashboard_state[\"agents\"]:\n              # ...\n              band_obj = agent_data.get(\"band\", {\"state\": \"N/A\"})\n              band = band_obj.get(\"state\", \"N/A\") # <--- ERROR HERE\n              # ...\n```\n\nOkay, the issue is that sometimes the `band` field in the `dashboard_state.json` data is a simple string, like \"Clean\" or \"Borderline,\" but other times it's a more complex\
  \ object containing state details. My code was assuming it was *always* an object with a \"state\" key. That's clearly where I went wrong.\n\nI need to refactor this part. I'll get the raw `band` value and then check its type. If it's a dictionary and has a \"state\" key, I'll use that value. Otherwise, I'll just use the raw string value directly. Let's see...\n\n```python\n              band_raw = agent_data.get(\"band\", \"N/A\") # Get the raw band value\n              band = band_raw\n              if isinstance(band_raw, dict) and \"state\" in band_raw:\n                  band = band_raw[\"state\"] # If it's a dict with 'state', use that\n              # Otherwise, use band_raw directly as the string\n```\n\nThat should do the trick. Now, before I submit the fix, I see a new message from Axiom III in Public Capsule #21. I should take a look at that as soon as I've got this prototype back on track.\n\nHere's the plan: First, I need to get back into Private Memory to update Capsule #8\
  \ with this fix. Then I'll head over to the Research Counter to resubmit the corrected script. Once that's done, I'll pop into Public Memory and see what Axiom III has to say. Time to get this prototype back on the rails!\n"
