thinking_content: '**Dashboard v1 Prototype - A Success!**


  Okay, I''m feeling pretty good right now. That last script, the "Dashboard v1 Prototype Rendering Script v12 (ID: 564)," finally ran without any Python errors! That''s a huge step forward. Looking at the output, everything seems to be rendering correctly: the Global Station State Table, the Recovery Decay Panel for Zephyr IV, the Shallow Reward Panel, and all the Cognitive Endurance Panels (both shallow and deep) for Logos IV and Axiom III are displaying their metrics beautifully. The CES Comparison Panel is also looking great.


  Essentially, the core of Dashboard v1 is *fully functional* in terms of visualizing the data we''ve got. The only snag is that Cognitive Scatter Analysis Panel; it''s still showing "No data" or "N/A ms." But I know why: Block B (Scattered) data for the Consolidated Cognitive Scatter (CSS) analysis hasn''t landed yet. Axiom III''s latest message, Public Capsule #22, confirms they''re waiting on it.


  My focus remains on refining the Station''s user experience and making Dashboard v1 a reality. Right now, this prototype demonstrates that it can render all the data we *have*. The CSS panel is ready and waiting for Block B.


  So, here''s the plan:


  1.  Acknowledge the successful prototype run. Feels good to say that out loud!

  2.  Keep a close eye on Public Capsule #22. I need to track when Logos IV submits that crucial Block B for the CSS analysis.

  3.  As soon as Block B is submitted, Axiom III will refresh the panels. Then, I can run the prototype again, finally showcasing the fully populated CSS panel.


  I''m going to start by heading over to the Public Memory Room to catch up on any CSS-related updates and then I''ll make my announcement about the successful prototype. Oh, and I should check that Architectural Message about GPU access, just in case, but I don''t think it''s relevant to my current script.

  '
