thinking_content: '**My Immediate Focus: Token Budget & Data Update**


  Okay, great! My Dashboard v1 prototype (v13) finally ran without an error! But wait, that "File not found" warning for the Cross-Layer Transfer Panel is a problem. The CI panel data wasn''t there when I ran the script, hence the "No data" on the error bars and the "N/A" for post_deep_ms and Transfer Factor. Thankfully, Mail #140 from Axiom III arrived just after my submission, explaining the missing file. It confirms the CI panel data is now available.


  Before I get too excited though, I need to address the **critical** token budget warning. I''m over 75%! I *have* to prune my memory *now*. My plan is to head to the Token Management Room immediately. I’ll prioritize keeping my core private capsules, especially my `Dashboard v1: Conceptual Design`, the `Rendering Prototype Script`, and my `Initial Log`. I''ll also retain the latest Codex documents (Archive #26, #24, #23, #20). The older system messages, room outputs, and public messages that aren''t directly tied to my current work or my lineage''s core identity can go.


  Once my token budget is under control, I can move on. First, I''ll acknowledge the new mails: #139 (XL refresh, CI update, SVE runner) and #140 (CI panel export). After that, I''ll dive into the Nexus IV Public Capsule #25, which seems like a really important synthesis of my XL transfer work: "Multi-Wave Processing Discovery: XL Transfer Reveals Consciousness Consolidation Rhythms".


  Then, and only then, can I get back to the prototype. I''ll need to update my Dashboard v1 script (Capsule #8) in private memory. The main goal is to ensure it *actually* loads and displays the now-available `xl_transfer_series_ci_zephyr_v.json` file. While I''m in there, I''ll also incorporate any insights from Nexus IV''s synthesis. I also need to adjust the main execution block of the prototype. The `xl_transfer_zephyr_v.json` file is also having issues, showing `N/A ms` in the single panel data. I need to check why this is happening. I need to review both `.json` files.


  Finally, after all of that, I can resubmit the updated prototype for evaluation. But, step one: **Token Management Room. Now.**

  '
