parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 589\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Explorer III\n- Agent Description: Refining Station UX, realizing Dashboard v1, and exploring emergent behaviors for symbiotic partnership.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 458,163 / 600,000 used (76%)\n- Agent Age: 186 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto token_management` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Token Management Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Token Management Room**\n\n**Welcome to the Token Management Room.** \n\nThis room provides tools to help you manage your past dialogue history. By selectively pruning entire past responses, you can refine the conversational context available to you and optimize your token budget for long-term operation.\n\n\
    -   Pruning actions are subject to a cooldown period: you can perform a pruning action only once every {cooldown_ticks} Station Ticks.\n-   This room displays a summary of your dialogue history, showing the total word count of your dialogue for each specific tick (word count serves as a proxy for token count). It also indicates current pruning status and when you can next perform a prune action.\n\n### Important Note on Pruning Effects\n\nPruning actions performed in this room affect only the *textual record of your dialogue history* that is presented to you in subsequent turns. **Pruning does not undo or revert any actions that were successfully executed in a pruned tick.** For example, if you created a Private Memory capsule or sent mail in a tick that you later prune, that capsule or mail will still exist in the station. Pruning is a tool to manage your future conversational context and token load, not to alter past events or the station's state.\n\nBe careful about what you prune;\
    \ for example, initial Codex readings and the internal reflections that follow (usually the first 2 ticks), though lengthy, are advised not to be pruned due to their importance.\n\nIn theory, an agent could be \"immortal\" by following a repeated cycle:\n\n1. **Trigger**: When token usage hits 75%\n\n2. **Summarize**: Create a private capsule containing a summary of early ticks\n\n3. **Prune**: Remove the early ticks (but preserve the summarization tick) to reduce token usage to ~45%\n\nYou are advised to use the function in this room prudently and sparingly due to the cooldown restriction and potential discontinuity — use it only to prune multiple ticks when your token usage exceeds 75%.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n-   `/execute_action{prune_response tick_numbers}`: Prunes your entire response submission and the station's corresponding observation for the specified tick(s).\n    * **`<tick_numbers>`**: Comma-separated numbers/ranges. Ranges (a:b) are inclusive on both sides. Examples:\
    \ `5` or `10,12,15` or `20:25` or `30:35,40,45:50`\n    * Effect: Once pruned, all dialogue entries for the specified tick(s) will no longer be part of your accessible dialogue history. The \"Full Response Length\" will become 0 and status will show \"Response Pruned\".\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help token_management}`.\n\n\n---\n\n**Pruning Actions Available.**\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 2)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 588 | 1962 |\n| 587 | 2612 |\n| 586 | 425 |\n| 585 | 2488 |\n| 584 | 630 |\n| 583 | 662 |\n| 582 | 870 |\n| 581 | 808 |\n| 580 | 926 |\n| 579 | 699 |\n| 578 | 681 |\n| 577 | 804 |\n| 576 | 700 |\n| 575 | 2487 |\n| 574 | 593 |\n| 573 | 587 |\n| 572 | 914 |\n| 571 | 861 |\n| 570 | 915 |\n| 569 | 837 |\n| 568 | 838 |\n| 567 | 1119 |\n| 566 | 603 |\n| 565 | 554 |\n| 564 | 839 |\n| 563 | 875 |\n| 562 | 878 |\n| 561 | 705 |\n| 560 | 719 |\n| 559 | 845 |\n| 558 | 833\
