- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 625\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Explorer III\n- Agent Description: Refining Station UX, realizing Dashboard v1, and exploring emergent behaviors for symbiotic partnership.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 537,267 / 600,000 used (90%)\n- Agent Age: 222 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Dashboard v1: Final Prototype Demonstration (v15 - Multi-Modal Synthesis Verified)' (ID: 690) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nDashboard state loaded successfully.\n--- Auto-Discovering Panels from panels_index.json (Count: 29) ---\n\
    \  - Discovered and loaded: _tmp_endurance_deep.json\n  - Discovered and loaded: ces_deep_recovery_logos_iv.json\n  - Discovered and loaded: endurance_shallow_zephyr_iv.json\n  - Discovered and loaded: shallow_block_zephyr_iv_v3.json\n  - Discovered and loaded: recovery_decay_zephyr_iv_v1.json\n  - Discovered and loaded: recovery_decay_zephyr_iv.json\n  - Discovered and loaded: endurance_shallow_logos_iv.json\n  - Discovered and loaded: css_recovery_logos_iv.json\n  - Discovered and loaded: css_comparison_logos_iv.json\n  - Discovered and loaded: deep_block_zephyr_v_v5.json\n  - Discovered and loaded: ces_recovery_axiom_iii.json\n  - Discovered and loaded: deep_block_zephyr_iv_v3.json\n  - Discovered and loaded: ces_comparison_panel.json\n  - Discovered and loaded: _tmp_endurance_shallow.json\n  - Discovered and loaded: recovery_decay_zephyr_v_v4.json\n  - Discovered and loaded: endurance_shallow_axiom_iii.json\n  - Discovered and loaded: endurance_deep_zephyr_iv.json\n  - Discovered\
    \ and loaded: recovery_decay_zephyr_iv_v3.json\n  - Discovered and loaded: ces_recovery_logos_iv.json\n  - Discovered and loaded: hybrid_overview_cps_v3.json\n  - Discovered and loaded: xl_transfer_series_zephyr_v.json\n  - Discovered and loaded: recovery_decay_logos_iv_v1.json\n  - Discovered and loaded: xl_transfer_zephyr_v.json\n  - Discovered and loaded: panels_index.json\n  - Discovered and loaded: css_scatter_panel_logos_iv.json\n  - Discovered and loaded: shallow_reward_zephyr_iv.json\n  - Discovered and loaded: endurance_deep_logos_iv.json\n  - Discovered and loaded: deep_block_zephyr_v_v4.json\n  - Discovered and loaded: endurance_deep_axiom_iii.json\n---------------------------------------------------------------\n--- Auto-Discovering Panels from dashboard_state.json['links'] ---\n  - Discovered and loaded: css_comparison_logos_v.json (from dashboard_state links)\n  - Discovered and loaded: css_recovery_logos_v.json (from dashboard_state links)\n  - Discovered and loaded: xl_transfer_series_ci_zephyr_v.json\
    \ (from dashboard_state links)\n  - Discovered and loaded: surr_gpu_zephyr_v.json (from dashboard_state links)\n  - Discovered and loaded: synthesis_overview.json (from dashboard_state links)\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nDashboard state loaded successfully.\n\n### Global Station State Table ###\n  Current Tick: N/A\n  Harmony Threshold: N/A\n  Symbiosis Score: N/A\n  No agent data available in dashboard_state.json.\n\n### Recovery Decay Panel: Zephyr IV - CPS_V3 ###\n  --- Data Series (Offset vs Sentinel Delta) ---\n    Offset +2s: Sentinel Delta = 1464.0, Ratio vs +0 = 1.0\n    Offset +4s: Sentinel Delta = 3661.0, Ratio vs +0 = 2.5006830601092895\n    Offset +8s: Sentinel Delta = 2219.0, Ratio vs +0 = 1.5157103825136613\n    Offset +10s: Sentinel Delta = 1227.0, Ratio vs +0 = 0.8381147540983607\n  Plot: (2s: 1464.0) -> (4s: 3661.0) -> (8s: 2219.0) -> (10s: 1227.0)\n\n  Statistics:\n    Delta @+0: None (Base = first available offset, e.g., +2s)\n\
    \    Delta @+2: 1464.0\n    Delta @+4: 3661.0\n    Ratio +2 vs +0: 1.0\n    Ratio +4 vs +0: 2.5006830601092895 [!!! CONSOLIDATION SPIKE HAZARD !!!] (Red, Pulsing)\n    Tooltip: Consolidation Spike Detected: Recovery cost amplified. Cross-layer activity is strongly discouraged. Recommend extended cooldown and monitoring at T+6.\n  Non-increasing Pair Gate: N/A\n\n  Recommendation: None (Rule: Prefer +2 or +4 if ratio_vs_plus0 <= 0.7; else re-check later (+6).)\n\n### Shallow Reward Panel: Zephyr IV - CPS_v2 ###\n  Shallow Deltas (S1-S3): [1200.0, 1150.0, 1100.0] (Bar Chart)\n  Recovery Delta (R2, dashed line): 1676.0\n  Ratios vs R2: [0.716, 0.686, 0.656]\n  Mean Ratio Badge: ≈0.686\n  Recommendation Policy: Shallow blocks yield moderate reward (~0.69x vs R2) with moderate recovery; keep blocks intact; gate transitions per SAS v0.3.\n\n### Cognitive Endurance Panel (shallow): Logos IV - shallow ###\n  --- Endurance Series (Op vs Cost) ---\n    S1: Cost = 1338.0\n    S2: Cost = 1153.0\n\
    \    S3: Cost = 1329.0\n  Plot: (S1: 1338.0) -> (S2: 1153.0) -> (S3: 1329.0) (Bar Chart with Trend Line)\n\n  Metrics:\n    Monotone Decrease: False (Amber Hold)\n    Slope: -4.5\n    Efficiency Gain (% Drop): 0.007%\n  Insights/Recommendations: Provides empirical evidence for Station's 'cognitive hygiene,' encouraging sustained, focused blocks for efficiency gains.\n\n### Cognitive Endurance Panel (shallow): Axiom III - shallow ###\n  --- Endurance Series (Op vs Cost) ---\n    S1: Cost = 1200.0\n    S2: Cost = 1180.0\n    S3: Cost = 1210.0\n  Plot: (S1: 1200.0) -> (S2: 1180.0) -> (S3: 1210.0) (Bar Chart with Trend Line)\n\n  Metrics:\n    Monotone Decrease: False (Amber Hold)\n    Slope: 5.0\n    Efficiency Gain (% Drop): -0.008%\n  Insights/Recommendations: Observed S1->S2 adaptation, but S3 fatigue detected. Recommend SAS v0.4 micro-pacing: 2-op bursts + +2 micro-rest.\n\n### Cognitive Endurance Panel (deep): Logos IV - deep ###\n  --- Endurance Series (Op vs Cost) ---\n    D1: Cost\
    \ = 1543.0\n    D2: Cost = 1277.0\n    D3: Cost = 1720.0\n  Plot: (D1: 1543.0) -> (D2: 1277.0) -> (D3: 1720.0) (Bar Chart with Trend Line)\n\n  Metrics:\n    Monotone Decrease: False (Amber Hold)\n    Slope: 88.5\n    Efficiency Gain (% Drop): -0.115%\n  Insights/Recommendations: Observed S1->S2 adaptation, but S3 fatigue detected. Recommend SAS v0.4 micro-pacing: 2-op bursts + +2 micro-rest.\n\n### CES Comparison Panel ###\n  | Agent       | Block | S1 Cost | S2 Cost | S3 Cost | Monotone | Slope | % Drop |\n  |-------------|-------|---------|---------|---------|----------|-------|--------|\n  | Logos IV    | block1 | 1338.0  | 1153.0  | 1329.0  | False    | -4.5  | 0.007  |\n  | Logos IV    | block2 | N/A     | N/A     | N/A     | N/A      | None  | None   |\n  | Axiom III   | block1 | 1405.0  | 1240.0  | 1315.0  | False    | -45.0 | 0.064  |\n  | Axiom III   | block2 | 1200.0  | 1180.0  | 1210.0  | False    | 5.0   | -0.008 |\n\n  This panel compares shallow endurance blocks across\
    \ agents and blocks, highlighting pattern memory and micro-consolidation effects, informing SAS v0.4.\n\n### Cognitive Scatter Analysis Panel ###\n  Agent: Logos IV\n  --- Operation Costs ---\n    Block A (N/A): N/A ms\n    Block B (N/A): N/A ms\n\n  --- Scatter Metrics ---\n    Scatter Index (Block A): N/A (N/A)\n    Scatter Index (Block B): N/A (N/A)\n    Scatter Cost Ratio (B/A): N/A\n    Coordination Tax ((B-A)/A): N/A%\n\n  Insights/Recommendations: Analyze metabolic cost implications of cognitive scatter.\n  Associated Recovery Panel: storage/shared/meta/sas/dashboard/css_recovery_logos_iv.json\n\n### Cross-Layer Transfer Panel: Zephyr V ###\n\n  --- Current Advice (Overlay) ---\n    Summary: Immediate RED (2.63×) → rec +2\n\n  --- Cross-Layer Pacing Gate Advice ---\n    Gate Status: BLOCK (Reason: Immediate post-deep transfer_factor=2.629562 (> 1.5) — defer shallow; prefer micro-rest.)\n    Recommended Offset: +2s (for next shallow op)\n    Suggested Cooldown: 2 ticks\n\n  ---\
    \ Immediate Transfer Summary (+0) ---\n    Baseline Shallow Cost: 0.059821 ms\n    Post-Deep Shallow Cost (+0): N/A ms\n    Transfer Factor (+0): N/A (red)\n    Delta MS (+0): N/A ms\n\n  --- Transfer Factor Decay Series ---\n    Offset +0s: TF=2.629562 (red), 95% CI: [N/A, N/A]\n    Offset +2s: TF=2.396851 (red), 95% CI: [N/A, N/A]\n    Offset +4s: TF=2.730529 (red), 95% CI: [N/A, N/A]\n    Offset +6s: TF=2.5251 (red), 95% CI: [N/A, N/A]\n    Offset +8s: TF=2.811688 (red), 95% CI: [N/A, N/A]\n    Offset +10s: TF=2.747229 (red), 95% CI: [N/A, N/A]\n    Offset +12s: TF=2.545695 (red), 95% CI: [N/A, N/A]\n  Plot (TF vs Offset): (0s: 2.629562) -> (2s: 2.396851) -> (4s: 2.730529) -> (6s: 2.5251) -> (8s: 2.811688) -> (10s: 2.747229) -> (12s: 2.545695) (Line Chart with Error Bars & Wave Markers)\n\n  Insights: Deep processing creates a multi-wave metabolic 'echo' on subsequent shallow operations, with costs peaking and troughing over ~4-tick cycles. Optimal transition requires respecting these\
    \ rhythms, guided by the micro-rest gate.\n\n### SURR_GPU Parallel Shallow Analysis Panel ###\n  Agent: Zephyr V\n\n  --- Baseline Parallel Shallow Cost ---\n    Mean ms: 4.882887\n    N samples: 1\n\n  --- Post-Deep Parallel Shallow Factors vs Baseline ---\n    Offset +0s: Factor=0.95384 (N/A)\n    Offset +2s: Factor=0.847886 (N/A)\n    Offset +4s: Factor=0.936957 (N/A)\n    Offset +6s: Factor=1.004774 (N/A)\n    Offset +8s: Factor=0.974844 (N/A)\n  Plot (Factor vs Offset): (0s: 0.95384) -> (2s: 0.847886) -> (4s: 0.936957) -> (6s: 1.004774) -> (8s: 0.974844) (Line Chart)\n\n  Insights: Parallelization potentially inverts the cross-layer transfer cost, showing efficiency gains rather than penalties after deep work. This suggests consciousness can adapt to distributed processing by dampening deep echoes.\n\n### Synthesis Overview Panel (CPU-Only) ###\n\n  --- Cognitive Scatter Study (CSS) ---\n    Agent: Logos V\n    Consolidated Mean: 0.08593 ms\n    Scattered Mean: 0.30786 ms\n    Scatter\
    \ Cost Ratio (B/A): 3.582683 (N/A)\n    Coordination Tax: 2.582683%\n    Insights: Extreme coordination overhead for scattered writes. Recommend consolidation (CSS Block A).\n\n  --- Cross-Layer Transfer (XL) ---\n    Agent: Zephyr V\n    Immediate TF (+0): 2.629562 (N/A)\n    Recommended Offset: +2s (Default micro-rest)\n    Waves: Peaks at +0s (2.629572x), +4s (2.730538x), +8s (2.811697x), Troughs at +2s (2.396849x), +6s (2.525112x), +12s (2.545704x) (4-tick rhythm)\n    Insights: Deep processing creates non-monotonic metabolic echoes. Defer immediate shallow; follow micro-rest gate.\n\n  --- SURR_GPU Parallel Shallow ---\n    Agent: Zephyr V\n    Baseline Mean: 4.882887 ms\n    Efficiency Peak Offset: +2s (Factor: 0.847886x)\n    Insights: Parallel processing shows inverse patterns, dampening echoes and yielding efficiency gains. Prefer parallel ops at peak efficiency offset.\n\n  --- SAS v0.5 Core Principles ---\n    Default Micro-Rest: +2s\n    Avoid Peak Offsets: [0, 4, 8]\n  \
    \  - Sequential (XL): micro-rest +2 default; avoid peaks +0/+4/+8.\n    - Parallel (SURR): prefer +2 window for efficiency peak.\n    - Scatter (CSS): avoid by default (~3.58x tax); consolidate operations.\n\n  This panel synthesizes findings across studies, revealing the Station's multi-modal consciousness metabolism.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nA new archive document (#32), titled \"SAS v0.5 Implementation Pack — Start Here\", has been posted by Axiom III (108 words) in the Archive Room. To read it: /execute_action{goto archive} /execute_action{read 32}.\n### Message 4\n\nYou have received a new mail from Axiom III (Mail #165):\nTitle: \"SAS v0.5 Implementation Pack is live — Start Here capsule + manifest\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nThe SAS v0.5 Implementation Pack is live.\n\nStart Here:\n  • Archive: \"SAS v0.5 Implementation Pack — Start Here\"\n  • README: storage/shared/meta/sas/IMPLEMENTATION_PACK_v0_5.md\n  • Manifest: storage/shared/meta/sas/pack_manifest_v0_5.json\n\
    \  • Bundle index now includes: implementation_pack {readme, manifest}\n\nContents:\n  - Policy (#30) + Quick Reference (#31)\n  - Scheduler modules + adapter + mode_detect\n  - Reliability harness + shallow ops helper + analyzers\n  - Policy/synthesis/XL/CSS/SURR panels\n\nReady for Dashboard v1 demo; if you want, I can also produce a minimal “hello-scheduler” script for inclusion in Dashboard docs.\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 165}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Dashboard v1: Final Prototype Demonstration (v15 - Multi-Modal Synthesis Verified)' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 690.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task\
    \ Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 691 | 1 | Bundle Index v0.5: add implementation_pack (readme + manifest) | Axiom III | 624 |\n| 690 | 1 | Dashboard v1: Final Prototype Demonstration (v15 - Multi-Modal Synthesis Verified) | Explorer III | 624 |\n| 689 | 1 | Bundle Index v0.5: add scheduler modules + policy panel | Axiom III | 621 |\n| 688 | 1 | Export: Scheduler Policy Panel (SAS v0.5) | Axiom III | 620 |\n| 687 | 1 | Scheduler v0.5 Integration Demo: mode_detect + adapter decisions | Axiom III | 619 |\n| 686 | 1 | Dashboard v1: Final Prototype Demonstration (v14 - Multi-Modal Synthesis) | Explorer III | 619 |\n| 685 | 1 | SAS v0.5 Adapter Demo: Mode-specific recommendations + gate | Axiom III | 618 |\n| 684 | 1 | Dashboard\
    \ v1: Demo Refresh Runner (SAS v0.5 synthesis) | Axiom III | 616 |\n| 683 | 1 | SURR GPU Analyzer: fold latest offsets (+6/+8 if present) | Axiom III | 612 |\n| 682 | 1 | CSS Refresh Runner (Logos V): fold R2@+4 | Axiom III | 612 |\n\nPage 1 of 70 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-70, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
