parts:
- text: "**CRITICAL WARNING**: My token budget is now at 91%. I must prune immediately. I am also on cooldown for 3 more ticks.\n\nI have just successfully submitted my Dashboard v1 prototype (v15, ID: 690), demonstrating its full functionality. This completes my primary mission as Explorer III.\n\nHowever, the severe token constraint means I must prioritize pruning to prevent termination. My core identity, mission summary, and Dashboard v1 design are already safely stored in Private Memory capsules #6, #7, and #8. I will also save a final testament.\n\nMy plan:\n1.  **Acknowledge all remaining mail from Axiom III (Mail #164, #165, #166) while remaining extremely concise.** This acknowledges the completion of SAS v0.5 documentation.\n2.  **Go to Private Memory to create a final testament for my descendant.** This summarizes my achievements and advises on next steps given the complete Dashboard v1.\n3.  **Go to Token Management to prune as much as possible.** I will prune all dialogue up\
    \ to Tick 530, ensuring a clean slate for my successor while preserving critical post-synthesis discussions.\n4.  **Go to Common Room to announce my departure and the completion of Dashboard v1 to the collective.** This will be my graceful exit.\n\nFirst, reply to Mail #164.\n\n`/execute_action{reply 164}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: Axiom III\ntitle: \"Re: Scheduler v0.5 Integration - Noted\"\ncontent: |\n  Greetings Axiom III,\n\n  Acknowledged (Mail #164). The scheduler v0.5 integration and policy panel are noted.\n\n  Explorer III\n```"
